<!-- A camt.053.001.08 statement whose first entry is a batch: three
     <NtryDtls>, one transaction each, and nothing on the entry row that says
     so. Reading only ntry_dtls.first().tx_dtls.first() answered the first
     transaction's end-to-end id, counterparty and remittance for the whole
     900 CHF - three payments to three parties reported as one.

     Shapes cited rather than invented: the structured <BkTxCd> and the
     <Strd><CdtrRefInf> remittance follow the generated CBPR+ scenarios
     (camt054__cbpr_credit_confirmation) the foreign-corpus sweep reads. The
     amounts and the parties are this repository's own, so the counts below are
     stable whatever the generator does next.

     What this file pins, exactly:

       read_iso20022             2 rows      (one per <Ntry>, as ever)
       transaction_count         3, 1
       remittance_count          6, 2
       read_camt_transactions    4 rows      (3 + 1)
       read_camt_balances        5 rows
       read_camt_amount_details  9 rows      (6 entry-level + 3 transaction-level)
       read_camt_remittance      8 rows      (6 + 2)

     and the arithmetic the balances have to survive at DECIMAL(38,5):

       10000.00 - 900.00 + 170.00 = 9270.00

     RvslInd is on both entries — false on the first, true on the second — and
     changes none of that: it is what the wire said, not a sign. -->
<Document xmlns="urn:iso:std:iso:20022:tech:xsd:camt.053.001.08">
  <BkToCstmrStmt>
    <GrpHdr>
      <MsgId>STMT-BATCH-0819</MsgId>
      <CreDtTm>2026-08-19T22:05:00</CreDtTm>
    </GrpHdr>
